  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Eleonora threatens to fire Mikhail Jekovich unless he restores order immediately, and sentences Senya and Fedya to work a week without pay and two weeks without days off. Mikhail immediately calls a buyer to get rid of the pony.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Быстро наведи в отеле порядок!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Иначе я тебя отсюда вышвырну.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А вы двое слушайте меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Неделю работаете совсем без зарплаты.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И две недели без выходных.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Всё, быстро пошли вон отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Нет, это я не вам.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Да, я срочно продаю пони.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ещё как продаю, жду вас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Айнура, быстро уберите всё здесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ainura",
      "t": "Я приехала работать в Москву.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "ainura",
      "t": "А теперь убираю за конём.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Быстро наведи в отеле порядок!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Quickly restore order in the hotel!' Eleonora anchors the line on 'quickly', while 'order' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Иначе я тебя отсюда вышвырну.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Otherwise I will throw you out of here.' The grammar packs 'otherwise' and 'I will throw out' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А вы двое слушайте меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And you two listen to me.' Notice how Russian expresses 'and' and 'me' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Неделю работаете совсем без зарплаты.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You will work a week with no salary at all.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'week' before landing on 'paychecks'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И две недели без выходных.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And two weeks without days off.' Eleonora brings out the contrast between 'and' and 'two' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Всё, быстро пошли вон отсюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'That is it, get out of here quickly!' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'everything' and finishing on 'from here'. Mikhail answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Нет, это я не вам.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, I did not mean that for you.' Mikhail brings out the contrast between 'no' and 'this' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Да, я срочно продаю пони.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, I am urgently selling a pony.' The meaning hinges on 'yes' working together with 'pony' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ещё как продаю, жду вас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I sure am selling it, I am waiting for you.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'else' and finishing on 'you'. Eleonora answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Айнура, быстро уберите всё здесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Ainura, quickly clean everything up here.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'Ainura' and finishing on 'here'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ainura",
      "t": "Я приехала работать в Москву.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I came to work in Moscow.' The grammar packs 'I' and 'Moscow' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ainura",
      "t": "А теперь убираю за конём.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And now I am cleaning up after a horse.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'and' before landing on 'horse'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
